WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:07.330
hi everyone I'm Sam Copeland with chess.com
recently we've launched a number of new features

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:12.440
and updates to game review and I'm here to
tell you all about them first up report cards

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.100
unlike the ones you get in school these are
fun and useful the first thing you'll see

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.260
is a summary from your coach describing how
the game went below that you will see a performance

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.000
rating for the game an estimate of your level
of play based on that single game previously

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.610
we've received a lot of questions about what
rating your accuracy for a particular game

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:39.230
might equal well this is that answer additionally
you'll get a quick grade for each phase of

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.820
the game based on your opening middle game
and in-game play grades are displayed as move

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.370
classifications ranging from blonder to brilliant
this should help you know exactly where you

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:58.540
need to improve and for more data check out
chess.com insights or chess.com stats next

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:03.550
up we've made two significant improvements
to classifications we have introduced a new

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:09.060
classification miss a Miss happens when a
player fails to take advantage of a tactical

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:15.670
opportunity such as finding Checkmate or punishing
an opponent's bad move however a Miss does

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:21.320
not indicate that the move you played was
a bad idea in general for example if you had

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:26.729
an advantage your opponent made an error allowing
a winning combination and you failed to find

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.840
the combination but you did keep your advantage
this would have been considered a mistake

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:38.270
or a blunder but now it will more accurately
be considered a Miss we've also recalibrated

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.810
how the blunder classification Works making
it more meaningful and useful now a blender

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:49.549
must not only drop the positions evaluation
significantly it must also lose material or

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:55.310
allow Checkmate we think this is how most
expert chess coaches would describe a blunder

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:00.950
it is not about some loss of eval according
to a computer it is about creating a tangible

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.909
exploitable opportunity for the opponent a
mostly behind the scenes Improvement is that

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:11.920
we have completely overhauled our book database
it should now better match well-known opening

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.019
Theory we've added known opening moves to
the book classification and we are removing

00:02:17.019 --> 00:02:23.300
book modes that are simply bad moves we've
also recognized that sometimes coaches feedback

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.240
can be hard to follow you can now have Coach
draw arrows and highlight squares over the

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.769
board to help you understand the advice you
can do this by hovering over or clicking on

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:39.459
the highlighted words in coach's explanation
of a particular move with this you can much

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:46.450
more easily visualize the pieces tactics and
ideas that coach refers to and last but certainly

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:52.420
not least we've given coach more in-depth
move explanations coach now helps you to see

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:58.000
all of the threats behind each move and whether
those threats are prevented or allowed the

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.780
coach will also mention specific pieces so
you'll know if coach is talking about a night

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:09.120
Bishop Rook or any other piece we are constantly
working to improve coach's explanations so

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.379
if you haven't taken a close look at the explanations
lately give them another try and let us know

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:20.269
what you think the new game review experience
is available on chess.com right now and look

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:30.980
for all of these features to make their way
into the apps later this year foreign

